     This aawwkk recognizes only the options -yy, -FF, and -ff.

     A program consisting only of BBEEGGIINN actions reads no input.
     When the field separator is not a blank, every occurrence of
     it ends a field, so empty fields are kept: with -FF: the
     record aa:bb::dd has four fields, and sspplliitt with an explicit
     separator behaves the same way.  Unlike other awks, con-
     catenation binds looser than the comparison operators here
     (and tighter than nothing else), so aa bb == aabb concatenates aa
     with the result of the comparison; parenthesize a concatena-
     tion that is to be compared.



